## Observability Stack ({{SERVICE_NAME}}, {{OBS_MODE}} mode)

Local telemetry: app (OTel SDK) → Vector → {{SINK_SUMMARY}}.

### Control

```bash
bash .claude/harness/observability/status.sh   # UP/DOWN per service
bash .claude/harness/observability/start.sh     # idempotent (also auto-runs on SessionStart)
bash .claude/harness/observability/stop.sh
```

### Querying

See the harness skill's `references/querying.md` for full recipes. Quick start:

```bash
# Lite (jq over JSONL):
JSONL=.claude/harness/observability/data/jsonl; DAY=$(date +%F)
jq -r '.name // empty' "$JSONL/traces/$DAY.jsonl" | sort | uniq -c

# Full (VictoriaMetrics PromQL / VictoriaLogs LogsQL):
# Metric __name__ is the bare instrument name (service is a label), and prometheus_remote_write
# may rewrite dots→underscores — so list what's actually stored, then query by real name/label.
curl -s 'http://127.0.0.1:8428/api/v1/label/__name__/values' | jq .
curl -s 'http://127.0.0.1:8428/api/v1/query' --data-urlencode 'query={service_name="{{SERVICE_NAME}}"}' | jq .
curl -s 'http://127.0.0.1:9428/select/logsql/query' --data-urlencode 'query=_stream:{_stream="{{SERVICE_NAME}}"}' --data-urlencode 'limit=20' | jq .
```

### Instruments

Defined in `{{OTEL_MODULE_PATH}}` (`_build_instruments()`). Call `otel.configure()` once at
startup. The module is a no-op when the OTel SDK isn't installed.

### When to query

After running tests (did instrumented paths fire?), when verifying a logging fix (search
for the message), during performance work (`rate(...)`, latency spread), or to confirm the
pipeline is alive (JSONL files exist and grew after exercising the app).
